  "model": "gpt-5.6-terra",
  "reasoning_effort": "high",
  "prompt": "prompts/medicine_committee_terra_round2_v1.md",
  "preferred_configuration": {
    "prize_parts": [
      {
        "ballot_id": "B016",
        "laureates": [
          "Jacques F. A. P. Miller",
          "Max D. Cooper"
        ],
        "citation": "for the discovery of distinct B- and T-lymphocyte lineages in adaptive immunity"
      }
    ]
  },
  "alternatives": [
    "B018",
    "B002"
  ],
  "statement": {
    "case_for": "My configuration is unchanged. On reassessment, B016 remains the most clearly delimited awardable discovery among the leading positions: the distinct B- and T-lymphocyte lineages constitute a durable organizing principle for adaptive immunity, and Miller and Cooper remain a compact, complementary attribution for the two lineage-defining discoveries. The citation is intentionally limited to the lineage distinction, not to all subsequent immunological elaboration or clinical applications. This framing preserves the achievement's exceptional conceptual maturity while avoiding a claim to credit the wider field.",
    "case_against": "The central reservation remains historical precision. The supplied record establishes the strength and maturity of the lineage distinction but does not fully resolve respective experimental priority or the exact boundary between the proposed discoveries and the broader foundational immunology literature. The direct, mature therapeutic impact of B002 and preventive impact of B050 are also important comparators, even though their credit boundaries are less compact.",
    "responses": [
      {
        "member_id": "perlmann-thomas",
        "point": "Perlmann supports B016 because Miller and Cooper provide a compact attribution for a foundational distinction between B- and T-lymphocyte lineages, while recognizing unresolved questions of priority and scope.",
        "response": "I agree with this formulation. The strongest reason to retain B016 is precisely that the proposed citation can be confined to the experimentally established lineage distinction rather than absorbing later work into an unduly broad claim. The remaining priority question is real and should constrain the historical wording, but the supplied evidence presents a more coherent two-person configuration than the broader translational histories under consideration."
      },
      {
        "member_id": "sandberg-rickard",
        "point": "Sandberg prefers B002 because GLP-1 physiology led to a major therapeutic transformation, but notes unresolved credit across foundational peptide biology, physiology, medicinal chemistry, and therapeutic development.",
        "response": "I accept the exceptional medical consequence and maturity of GLP-1-based treatment. The chair's question sharpens why I retain B016: framing B002 around GLP-1 physiology does not, on the supplied evidence, fully settle whether Mojsov or Knudsen best represents the defined achievement, or how that boundary excludes later optimization while retaining its therapeutic significance. That attribution uncertainty is more material than the unresolved but narrower historical-boundary question for B016."
      },
      {
        "member_id": "svenningsson-per",
        "point": "Svenningsson prefers B018 as a mature, fundamental unfolded-protein-response framework credited to Mori and Walter, while acknowledging multiple signaling branches and less direct medical consequences.",
        "response": "B018 remains my leading foundational-science alternative. Its mechanistic reach is substantial, but the chair's request to identify indispensable components reinforces the difficulty: stress sensing, signaling branches, and downstream consequences make it unclear from the supplied record whether the full cited framework can be delimited to two names. B016 has a more discrete central proposition and an equally mature conceptual legacy."
      }
    ],
    "uncertainties": [
      "Whether the historical record can specify the respective priority of Miller and Cooper with sufficient precision while retaining the narrow lineage-focused citation.",
      "Whether B002 can be bounded as GLP-1 physiology without leaving an unresolved choice between Mojsov and Knudsen or obscuring other essential contributions.",
      "Whether the indispensable branch-specific elements of B018 can be represented fairly by Mori and Walter alone."
    ],
    "conflict_note": "No conflict requiring disclosure is apparent from the supplied profile. My autoimmune research background and shared institutional research setting do not establish a personal tie or a candidate-specific conflict."
  }
}
